WEBVTT

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.330
I will do it.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:30.620
No way.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.290
I didn't think you'd really
kill him, Miss Yumiko.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.830
Go back, Kouta.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:44.830
If you give an honest report,
I'm sure they won't kill you.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.290
For a guy like this...

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:27.950
"AFTERLOST"

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:37.330
"Episode 2: Sacrifice"

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:42.750
It must feel pretty pathetic to be saved by me.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.700
Kouta...

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.870
The girl...

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:51.000
Wasn't there a girl with me...?

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:03.040
She only has a few scrapes.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.540
Are you really planning on saving this guy?

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.120
Forget about me.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.120
Please, just save the girl.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.450
Or this'll all be meaningless.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.910
This is meaningless for me, unless I save you.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.450
The Agency is going to take her back.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.950
You're going to walk away from this.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:26.040
Isn't that enough?

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:29.580
Then, I guess we're saving the both of them.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.410
Worry about the details later.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:32.580
Kouta!

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.080
We can't just abandon this girl here.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.950
"256: The police sirens are going crazy!"
"257: There was an accident on the expressway."
"258: A pile-up?"

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:52.330
"256: The police sirens are going crazy!"
"257: There was an accident on the expressway."
"258: A pile-up?"
The Metropolitan Police requests back-up.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.250
"259: I heard a helicopter went down."
"260: That's pretty serious."
"261: Did a news helicopter make a mistake?"
The Metropolitan Police requests back-up.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.870
"262: It was a military helicopter,
but I don't know the details."
"263: Whereabouts on the expressway?"
Immediate dispatch of removal team needed.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:57.370
"264: The lock-down district. As expected,
that area must be pretty crazy."
"265: There, huh...? That's no surprise."
Immediate dispatch of removal team needed.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:57.660
"264: The lock-down district. As expected,
that area must be pretty crazy."
"265: There, huh...? That's no surprise."

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:58.660
"266: Doesn't sound like it was just an accident."

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:03.500
Takuya. You've got to be kidding...

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:23.200
I can't believe our detective office had an
outpost within the lock-down district.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.290
It was set up after you quit.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:30.790
It's the perfect place to
hide troublesome things.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.160
I'm sure this girl has gone through a lot.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:44.160
I can't believe she was imprisoned
there for three years.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.950
That's right. I still haven't
thanked you, Kouta.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:51.040
I didn't do it for you.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:55.450
Jeez, you really stuck your head
into something dangerous.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.160
It's the terms of the contract.

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:00.580
No matter what I say,
I know you won't stop, Takuya.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:02.330
But don't be so reckless.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:06.000
Right now, we need a way to
get out of the lock-down district.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.000
Got it.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.250
First, I want to fix my bike.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.540
Is there a way to get a hold of Geek?

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.500
I lost my cellphone somewhere.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:27.580
Geek?

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:32.290
You worked with him once.
He's a childhood friend.

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:35.580
Hold on, let me check the database.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.580
Are you talking about that shut-in fatty?

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.580
Geek isn't just a regular fatty.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:41.910
I'm sure he knows where my bike is right now.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.450
No good.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.750
It'll be faster if we bait him.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:51.580
"Poster: Homurin"
"A RL meeting, huh~ It's been
a long time. I can't wait."

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.410
"Poster: YMK"
"<i>Tenmusu </i>rice balls!"

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:56.040
"Poster: Geek"
"<i>Tenmusu </i>are so delicious!!
I love Yua-<i>tan </i>the best, too!!"

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.500
"Poster: Geek"
"<i>Tenmusu </i>are so delicious!!
I love Yua-<i>tan </i>the best, too!!"
There. Got him.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.410
"Poster: Geek"
"<i>Tenmusu </i>are so delicious!!
I love Yua-<i>tan </i>the best, too!!"
So fast!

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:03.660
Why don't we include him in our plans?

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:20.790
Don't move around so much.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:23.250
What if they find you?

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:30.660
Eat. You won't hold up.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.660
I'm sorry.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:33.830
Your injuries.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.040
Oh.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.200
Jeez, I got caught up in something
really troublesome.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.910
Well, don't worry about it.
All part of the contract.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.830
I'll take half.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:13.330
The guy who saved us on the expressway.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:16.330
Were you the one who called him there?

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:20.660
I don't know... But I know him.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:25.250
Akira... He was guarding my father.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:32.450
Bodyguard? Oh, a security officer.
If he appeared as a Tama-shi...

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:36.580
He was caught up in Lost.
Right in front of my eyes.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:40.250
Not just Akira.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:43.330
My father. My little brother.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:46.410
Everyone disappeared.

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:53.330
I see. I wonder what the hell it is. Lost.

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:56.660
Even now, we don't know if it
was a natural disaster or not.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:59.700
We don't know if it'll happen again.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.410
Do you know anything about it?

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.200
Must be past your bedtime.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:21.200
Don't make fun of me.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.330
Both in the afternoon and evening,

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:33.620
there was an isolated abnormality
of gravitational waves.

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:37.160
His appearance matches the timing
of the incident this afternoon.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.910
We've got it.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:44.410
Physical proof of Tama-shi appearance...

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.700
No good.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.750
Even all the back streets are being monitored.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:55.290
That means...

00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:58.000
Yes.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:02.950
Let's go.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:06.160
Hey! Why are you leading?!

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:11.000
He hasn't changed at all.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.950
Well, let's go.

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:16.120
Yes.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:43.040
You okay?

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.000
Yeah.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.910
We'll be at the next station in a few minutes.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:49.000
We'll be out of the lock-down district.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.790
Damn, they're really troublesome.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:56.540
Just what is the Agency? Does the
government or police have any idea?

00:09:56.540 --> 00:10:00.290
Even as members, we couldn't
get the whole picture.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:07.040
It was more like a society of like-minded
individuals than a large single-entity.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:10.040
It's a pretty creepy group.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:13.250
I really wish our office chose who
they worked with more carefully.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:29.200
Suzuna!

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:30.620
Shit!

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:33.620
After all, this is about all that
your brains can come up with.

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:39.700
Kouta.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:51.540
Hurry!

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:52.910
Huh?

00:10:57.830 --> 00:10:59.290
Miss Yumiko!

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:00.540
Yumiko!

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:09.660
Let's go, Kouta.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:17.620
There's no point trying to get through this way.

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:20.040
I have something to say to you.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.750
After them.

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:31.410
Now, then.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:38.540
Looks like you don't plan to talk.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:51.750
Shit!

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:57.410
Let's take them down, here!

00:11:57.410 --> 00:12:00.370
Huh? H-Hey!

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:08.790
Hey! Tell me, if you planned
to do something else--

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.450
You're ignoring me?!

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:23.160
You promised me!

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:26.700
You promised me Takuya's safety!

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.870
The higher-ups made their decision.

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:33.410
How nice. You don't have
to think for yourself at all.

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:35.910
And this is the result of thinking for yourself?

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:38.700
Then, you're the foolish one here.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:48.580
Why did you betray the Agency?
Don't you value your own life?

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:53.870
If I had to continue obeying them like that,
I'd choose freedom any day.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:57.540
Why would you go that far for that man?

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:00.700
Because I love him.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:04.200
Hide, Yuki!

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:07.450
Shit!

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:09.870
Take the right. I'll get the left.

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:15.160
Looks like you might be a little rusty, sir.

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:24.330
Well, even I could do that...

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:28.160
All right. We just need to get outside,
then we're out of the lock-down district!

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.660
Um, that person named Yumiko...

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:42.040
It's fine. She always thinks of ways
for everyone to make it out safely.

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:47.290
Even if we go up like normal,
the exit is closed off.

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:49.910
So we're going to take a little detour.

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:53.410
You've changed a bit.

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:54.830
Huh?

00:13:54.830 --> 00:14:00.040
You would have never taken such a
thankless job like this in the past.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:02.160
That so?

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:06.910
But, well. I think things are
more interesting this way.

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:08.000
Huh?

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:12.540
If I had to pick, I'd rather
do something interesting...

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:15.870
You, too. Haven't you changed a bit?

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:18.950
How so?

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:23.700
Well, it's fine if you can't tell.

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:31.290
It's here! This is it!

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:37.120
I'll tell you all of my
heroic stories later, Yuki.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:38.040
No need.

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:39.620
So cold.

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:41.870
Before our office went a little crazy,

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:45.080
the government gave us a
lot of important missions.

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:46.330
Hey!

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:50.000
It's fine! You're always too
gruff about everything!

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:51.830
So, that mission--

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:56.660
What is it, Kouta?

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.000
Huh?

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:01.750
Kouta!

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:26.120
Sir... Please, go...!

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:31.120
--Mr. Kouta!
--Come on!

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:32.910
No!!

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:44.450
This isn't interesting at all...

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:01.200
That hurts...

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:05.830
That hurts, dammit!

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:16.450
Wait!

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:22.000
Hey...

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.580
Why?

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:28.830
Why are you still going forward
like nothing happened?!

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:46.450
It's him!

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:50.750
Tama-shi?!

00:17:10.540 --> 00:17:12.290
Get on, you two!

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:20.500
As expected of you, Geek.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:23.330
But, we're heading back
toward the lock-down district.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:27.370
That's because something
weird is chasing after us!

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:31.040
Like a huge swarm of hornets!

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:34.540
What the hell is that?!

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:43.200
He's fixated on the knife...

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:45.080
Geek, is the bike functional?

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.790
I did some emergency repairs, but...

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.620
What are you planning to do?!

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:51.660
I'll distract him!

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:55.040
Use that chance to escape with Yuki!

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:58.200
What?! What are you saying?!

00:17:58.200 --> 00:17:59.200
Are you insane?!

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:00.700
Stop!

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:04.620
Why are you going this far?

00:18:06.370 --> 00:18:08.540
Because I want to.

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:17.500
Ah! W-Wait!

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:20.580
Let's do this, you little hornet bastard!

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:34.910
What are you doing...?!

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:37.120
What's the point, if you come along?!

00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:39.830
I'm sorry. But...

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:41.790
...I wanted to!

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:46.370
Please give me a bit of time!

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:50.830
I'm starting to get how this guy works.

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:52.500
Hang on tight, Yuki.

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:09.250
I thought so.

00:19:20.500 --> 00:19:24.040
You only attack with this knife.

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:27.290
You must be really attached to it.

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:31.290
Give... it... back...

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:37.910
Give... it... back...

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:08.700
Akira!

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:35.250
Now I can protect you.

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:40.040
Thank you, Akira.

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:47.910
Just now, you were able to call him...

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:57.040
Hey!

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:09.540
She's finally awakened.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:10.790
Huh?

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:14.950
Looks like I shouldn't
overwrite things any further.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:23.250
Thanks. You saved me.

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:26.000
No, I'm the one being saved.

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:29.410
To be honest, I have no way
of fighting the Tama-shi.

00:21:29.410 --> 00:21:34.620
I know this is a bit contradictory,
but I need your help to fulfill this contract.

00:21:36.450 --> 00:21:38.290
Will you help me?

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:40.830
Me, too.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:46.370
I want to go and confirm if my
father is alive with my own eyes.

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:52.910
Got it. First, let's go and
get Yumiko and Kouta.

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:37.950
"AFTERLOST"

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:46.620
Next Episode: "Memory."
